# Commit Message Format

For any action that creates or rewrites commit messages, including commit,
amend, merge, revert, cherry-pick, squash, and rebase, first run this in the
target repository:

```bash
git log -15 --format=%s
```

Match the new subject to the dominant pattern in that output, including
prefixes, scopes, ticket IDs, capitalization, and punctuation. Prefer recent
entries when patterns conflict and use formats supported by the repository
history.

When the history has no established pattern, use a concise one-line imperative
subject.
